## 3. Golden Paths "fail" on both PRs: cancellations, not failures
- #525: job 108045360295 is `conclusion: cancelled`, and its annotation reads "Canceling since a
  higher priority waiting request for golden-paths-dev-demo exists".
- #526: job 108045434526 is also `cancelled`.
- The golden-paths job is unchanged by this PR. Its `concurrency: golden-paths-dev-demo` group lets
  one run hold the shared Demo company, and a master push at 11:05 UTC took the slot. This is the
  pattern #454, #473, #474 and #506 merged under (fix.md, residual 1).

## 4. The head that merges
Later commits change only workflowRunsCiRule.ts, its unit test, docs, and the job timeout. The run on
the final head is recorded as a PR comment on #525. A commit cannot contain the record of its own run.

## Timeout
The measured job took 8m13s at load average ~45 on 32 cores. timeout-minutes is set to 30: about 3.5x
the measured time, for heavier load. It was 15, and the build alone did not fit that.
